QMD 5.0 4 (drop-in patches for OpenESC)

drop-in patches you can apply directly to an OpenESC checkout (or any ESC firmware repo).
The patch set does three simple things:
    1. Adds the QMD v5.0 kernel files (qmd5.h / qmd5.c) — pure C, no external deps, fixed-point Q12.20.
    2. Adds a tiny integration wrapper (qmd5_integration.c) that exposes a convenient float API for any part of the codebase that still uses floats (optional).
    3. Provides a Makefile/CMake snippet you can paste into your build files to compile the new files.
Save the patch and apply with git apply qmd5_openesc.patch from your repo root (or manually copy the new files into the paths below). I used conservative file-paths so you can drop them into the usual OpenESC firmware tree and then add the sources to your build system.

How to apply
From your repo root:
    1. Save the patch text below into a file, e.g. qmd5_openesc.patch.
    2. Run:
git apply qmd5_openesc.patch
    3. Add the new source files to your build system:
        ◦ If you use a Makefile, add src/qmd/qmd5.c and src/qmd/qmd5_integration.c to the SRCS list.
        ◦ If you use CMake, add add_library(qmd5 src/qmd/qmd5.c src/qmd/qmd5_integration.c) or append the .c files to the existing target.
    4. Rebuild the firmware. See usage examples below for integrating calls.

What the patch contains
    • src/qmd/qmd5.h — header public API
    • src/qmd/qmd5.c — fixed-point Q12.20 kernel and derivative
    • src/qmd/qmd5_integration.c — a tiny float wrapper + example qmd5_apply_to_tau() helper
    • docs/qmd5_README.md — mini README with usage notes
    • Makefile/CMake snippet (text in patch comments) — paste into your build system

