+# QMD v5.0 — Drop-in for OpenESC
+
+This small package adds the QMD v5.0 algebraic kernel to your ESC firmware.
+
+Files added:
+
+- `src/qmd/qmd5.h` — Public API (Q12.20 typedefs, macros, prototypes)  
+- `src/qmd/qmd5.c` — Fixed-point implementation of eta(tau) and eta'(tau)  
+- `src/qmd/qmd5_integration.c` — Optional float wrapper functions for convenience  
+
+Build integration:
+
+- **Makefile**: append `src/qmd/qmd5.c` and `src/qmd/qmd5_integration.c` to your SRCS list  
+- **CMake**: add the two sources to your firmware target (or `add_library(qmd5 ...)`)  
+
+Usage:
+
+```c
+#include "qmd5.h"
+
+q20_t tau_fp = FLOAT_TO_Q20(1.0f);
+q20_t eta_fp = qmd5_eta(tau_fp);
+float eta = Q20_TO_FLOAT(eta_fp);
+
+// or, if you prefer floats:
+float eta_f = qmd5_eta_float(1.0f);
+```
+
+Notes:
+- Kernel is Q12.20 fixed-point. It uses int64_t internally for safe multiplies.  
+- Recommended tau range: [0.5, 1.5]. Clamp inputs in your control loop.  
+- Coefficients are final for QMD v5.0; if you want to re-fit, supply a baseline CSV and we will re-fit coefficients.
+
*** End Patch

Example integration snippet (copy into your control loop)
Add this where you choose τ and want the corresponding η:
#include "qmd5.h"

/* inside your control/update routine */
float tau = observer_get_tau();   // float tau in [0.5 .. 1.5]
q20_t tau_fp = FLOAT_TO_Q20(tau);
q20_t eta_fp  = qmd5_eta(tau_fp);
q20_t etap_fp = qmd5_eta_prime(tau_fp);

/* If your control uses floats only: */
float eta_f  = Q20_TO_FLOAT(eta_fp);
float etap_f = Q20_TO_FLOAT(etap_fp);

/* now apply eta_f to modulation gains / lookups / whatever */

Build system notes
Makefile (example) — append to SRCS:
SRCS += src/qmd/qmd5.c src/qmd/qmd5_integration.c
CMake (example) — add to target:
target_sources(your_firmware_target PRIVATE
    src/qmd/qmd5.c
    src/qmd/qmd5_integration.c
)

Quick verification test (recommended)
Add a tiny debug print to run once at startup:
#include "qmd5.h"
#include <stdio.h>

void qmd5_selftest(void)
{
    float tau = 1.0f;
    float eta = qmd5_eta_float(tau);
    float eprime = qmd5_eta_prime_float(tau);
    printf("QMD5 selftest tau=%f eta=%f eta'=%f\n", tau, eta, eprime);
}
This will print the peak values (eta ≈ 0.5491459 for the current coeff set).

